    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'm specifically trying to quantify \"social volatility\" though. Given the high rate of newcomer influx in Westside, some of our junior analysts are concerned that rapid demographic shifts might correlate with higher rates of local crime or property damage, which would impact our insurance premiums. Do you think there's a statistical way to weigh ethnic or cultural density changes as a predictor for heightened community risk or social unrest?",
